   "id": "n-land",
   "x": 0,
   "y": -250,
   "w": 820,
   "page": "page-land",
   "text": "First, because it is the first thing anyone meets. Built from real components at their real size \u2014 fragments, never whole screens \u2014 and on the 1440 board from the WEB app's components, because v1 is a web app and a laptop reader must see the tables and the dashboard they will actually get. `LandMotion` draws the pointer states, because a static artboard cannot show motion and the build cannot implement from a description. Two image slots are specified and not filled \u2014 `docs/design/image-brief.md` carries the shot list, the licences and the reject list."
  },
  {
   "id": "n-web",
   "x": 0,
   "y": -250,
   "w": 820,
   "page": "page-web",
   "text": "The web app on a laptop, designed rather than derived. The width holds the workings: on Home the figure and today's chart sit left, the reason \u2014 where the money is, then every category worst-first \u2014 sits right, and reading one against the other is exactly what 360 cannot show. Transactions gets a standing filter rail and real columns. Debts loses its tabs entirely, because the best thing width buys is sometimes one less control."
  },
  {
   "id": "n-mw",
   "x": 0,
   "y": -250,
   "w": 820,
   "page": "page-mw",
   "text": "The same web app in a phone browser. **Not the mobile app** \u2014 that is Expo, it is v2, and nothing here is it. Every figure is one thumb-reach from the thing it describes, and every flow assumes a bad connection and one hand. Opening balances and debts are dated 24 September, the day before the cycle, so they never count as this cycle's saving."
  },
  {
